  41:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c **** /** @file h_npdu.c  Handles messages at the NPDU level of the BACnet stack. */
  42:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c **** 
  43:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c **** /** Handler for the NPDU portion of a received packet.
  44:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  Aside from error-checking, if the NPDU doesn't contain routing info,
  45:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  this handler doesn't do much besides stepping over the NPDU header
  46:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  and passing the remaining bytes to the apdu_handler.
  47:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  @note The routing (except src) and NCPI information, including
  48:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  npdu_data->data_expecting_reply, are discarded.
  49:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  * @see routing_npdu_handler
  50:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *
  51:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  * @ingroup MISCHNDLR
  52:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *
  53:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  * @param src  [out] Returned with routing source information if the NPDU
  54:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   has any and if this points to non-null storage for it.
  55:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   If src->net and src->len are 0 on return, there is no
  56:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   routing source information.
  57:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   This src describes the original source of the message when
  58:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   it had to be routed to reach this BACnet Device, and this
  59:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   is passed down into the apdu_handler; however, I don't
  60:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   think this project's code has any use for the src info
  61:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   on return from this handler, since the response has
  62:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *                   already been sent via the apdu_handler.
  63:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  @param pdu [in]  Buffer containing the NPDU and APDU of the received packet.
  64:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  *  @param pdu_len [in] The size of the received message in the pdu[] buffer.
  65:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_npdu.c ****  */
